# StockSearchInput tone (dashboard theme P0)

Vuetify `defaultTheme` is **light**. Do not mix per-control `theme="dark"` on the purple glass shell.

## Rules

- On **dark canvas** (watchlist, workbench): use `StockSearchInput` with `tone="on-dark"`.
- On **white card** pages (trade dialog, deep analysis): use `tone="on-light"` or omit (default is `on-light`).
- **Never** set `theme="dark"` on `v-text-field` or `StockSearchInput` — it enables `color-scheme: dark` and breaks typed text contrast.
- **Never** use Vuetify `color="white"` as input text color; use `tone` instead.
- Do not pass `bg-color` / `color` / `baseColor` to `StockSearchInput` for theming (deprecated).
- Do not use `input-class="stock-code-input"` as a theme switch; use `tone`.

